ty  and discuss problems of politics so  we we i got a fair sense of what his  visions were he seems to have been  pretty reckless i guess he was clueless  as  as  he i mean it wasn't a very effective  plot  and yet on the other hand if you're a  school teacher in south east hunan  trying to overthrow emperor jung jung  you know it's not a very easy thing to  do and one of the ways would be to um  locate a general who might back you and  another would be to  get the general to agree to  uh to move you know  and another would be to get somebody to  deliver a letter to the general anyway  who's surrounded by bodyguards and  outriders  uh how i mean you can't just walk into  the generals yaman and say  here's a secret letter because they it  would be torn open and then you'd be  run through with a knife you know i mean  you couldn't do it  uh or you'd be i mean you would never  reach the general so i think the the  teacher was extremely skillful in  delivering it on the road i think that  was the way to do it yeah if i'd had a i  would have delivered it on the road it  was your only chance to sort of run  across the road you're not going to get  general yay he's going to be guarded  around the clock and with very tough  people and his door keeper you know  you're not going to get through the  gates there's huge gates when you've  seen the chinese yarmouth you're not  going to get through that with a letter  so by running across the street he he he  actually got them got the man to read it  and then for a dizzying hour and a half  or more uh the general having read the  entire letter which was astounding not  just received it but read the entire  thing the general then says he's joined  the conspiracy so you must have been  wild with glee just for a little bit  you'd actually got two out of three of  the crucial status any trouble is he  then betrayed you uh but so you can't  get everything right  but two out of three is is pretty  remarkable for us a small village scho